findings.expected:
A photograph of the real lamp in this studio, at this exposure, would show the same reflections in the same places as faint lighter patches with clean, straight edges:
- the rectangle about 1-2 L* lighter and the trapezoids 0.3-0.7 lighter;
- slightly whitened: G and B up 10-20 levels, R up 2-3.
It would show no outline, no dashed seam, no line along the horizon, and a smooth glow.

The fix is in the denoise, not the studio. Re-denoise or re-render the lit frames with one of:
- albedo/normal guide passes that are prefiltered;
- guide passes that do not carry the reflected studio;
- enough samples to denoise lightly.

Core LIT-b uses the same pipeline. Unless this changes, it will keep the seams at about 0.9 of their L* strength. Check it with an R-channel high-pass before it goes up.

Lit by the ball's glow and this dim studio, the base should:
- be brightest at the lip and just under the ball;
- fall quickly to an even, deep red;
- stay red to its silhouette, with flanks at half to all of the centre;
- never go black;
- be lifted a little near the foot by the floor's red pool.

That is what it shows.

A rough check agrees. At this frame's studio level the studio alone gives the base front about L* 3.4-5.9: the OFF base's Y of 0.10-0.125 times the LIT/OFF wall ratio of 0.038-0.053. The ball adds a little on top.

Keep as is.

found.q1_ready:
Pendant LIT is ready as the Hemisphere's picture 2 at visitor sizes:
- the glow is even, Ember red, unclipped, with no LED spots;
- the lift lamp is off and the room reads as dim studio;
- the hairline outlines at full size are a fix.

Core LIT is not ready, as a final:
- the reflections on the ball render as pale crackle that reads as crazed acrylic at 480 (blocking);
- its floor's brightest part is a neutral studio light on the left, not the lamp (fix).

Both carry into LIT-b unless changed. Its base is fixed: maroon to the silhouette, flanks 0.43-0.77 of the centre. The planned -0.48 EV should land the glows within 2 L* (Core 1.3-1.6 under the pendant) and the walls within 3 L*, but not the floors.
